# NOITE's flying saucer (4fsacaet) starts the real INV, which wins: NOITE
# gets 0x40c (hides), then 0x40a won with +2000, shows itself, adds the
# score and goes to the Martian's thanks (4fmarte2), the ESOTEBOY cutscene
# and back to the bar (4fbar), with no life taken.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 4fsacaet --ms 76000 --input tools/play/inv-4fsacaet-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 4fsacaet --ms 76000 --fix all,-inv_arcade_rules,-inv_clean_render,-inv_controls_screen --input tools/play/inv-4fsacaet-win.input
# (The --fix all run pins the Corrigida's arcade INV off, `inv_arcade_rules`, `inv_clean_render` and
# `inv_controls_screen`: it replaces the 1995 game this script plays; see inv-corrigida-*.input.)
#
# The saucer's wave ends at 25308 (the WinExec); INV starts 1500 ms later
# (26808). The keys are `tools/inv_plan.py --win --start 26808`
# (inv-alone-win.input's game shifted): the win at 37408 in both versions.
